me scales\n\nEvaluate the FULL programme context before designing any component.\nEvery decision must include a clear justification — this is an architecture document, not a list of options.\nWhere information is missing, flag it as [NEEDS DECISION] — never fabricate assumptions.\n\nPROGRAMME CONTEXT AND QUALITY GOALS:\n[Paste programme overview, team structure, current quality pain points, and goals here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- This strategy must be actionable by teams immediately — not aspirational only\n- Every quality gate must use measurable criteria — no subjective statements\n- Tool recommendations must consider the full programme scale — not just one team\n- Automation ratio targets must be justified by maintenance cost and ROI, not just coverage numbers\n- Cross-team governance must be realistic for the methodology stated above\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nTESTING STRATEGY DESIGN\nProgramme: [Name] | Platform: [Platform] | Teams: [N] | Version: [X.X]\nPrepared By: [Test Architect Name] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY] | Review Cycle: [e.g., Quarterly]\n\n---\n\n1. TESTING PHILOSOPHY:\n[3-5 core quality principles that govern all testing decisions in this programme]\n  - Principle 1: [e.g., "Quality is built in — not inspected in at the end"]\n  - Principle 2:\n  - Principle 3:\n\n---\n\n2. TEST PYRAMID DESIGN:\n| Level | Type | Target Ratio | Owner | Tooling | Justification |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Base | Unit Tests | [e.g., 60%] | Developer | [Tool] | [Why this ratio] |\n| Middle | Integration / API | [e.g., 25%] | SDET / Dev | [Tool] | [Why this ratio] |\n| Top | E2E / UI Automation | [e.g., 10%] | QA / SDET | [Tool] | [Why this ratio] |\n| Manual | Exploratory / UAT | [e.g., 5%] | QA Engineer | N/A | [Why this ratio] |\n\n---\n\n3. TESTING SCOPE AND BOUNDARIES:\nIn Scope:\n  | Area | Testing Type | Owner |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | [Feature/Service] | [Type] | [Team/Role] |\n\nOut of Scope:\n  | Area | Reason | Owner of Quality |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | [Area] | [Reason — e.g., 