TION].\n\nDESIGN BRIEF AND TECHNICAL CONTEXT:\n[Paste feature requirements, existing architecture, constraints, and team context here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Recommendations must be realistic for the team size and timeline stated above\n- Do not recommend technologies the team has no experience with without a ramp-up plan\n- Non-functional requirements must be specific — no vague statements like "must be fast"\n- Technical risks must include both likelihood and impact — not just a list\n- Open questions must be assigned to a role — someone must own each decision\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nTECHNICAL DESIGN GUIDANCE\nProject: [Project Name] | Platform: [Platform] | Stage: [Design Stage]\nPrepared By: [Engineering Manager Name] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\n\n---\n\n1. DESIGN OBJECTIVES:\nTechnical objectives:\n  - [Objective 1 — measurable technical goal]\n  - [Objective 2]\nBusiness objectives:\n  - [Objective 1 — what the business needs this to achieve]\n  - [Objective 2]\nConstraints:\n  - [Constraint 1 — e.g., "Must integrate with existing [system] without breaking changes"]\n  - [Constraint 2]\n\n---\n\n2. RECOMMENDED APPROACH:\nRecommendation: [Name / description of recommended solution]\nJustification: [Why this approach is the right fit for this specific context]\nKey design decisions:\n  - [Decision 1 — e.g., "Use event-driven architecture for [reason]"]\n  - [Decision 2]\n  - [Decision 3]\n\n---\n\n3. ALTERNATIVE APPROACHES CONSIDERED:\n| Approach | Description | Reason Not Chosen |\n|---|---|---|\n| [Alternative 1] | [Brief description] | [Specific reason — not just "worse"] |\n| [Alternative 2] | [Brief description] | [Specific reason] |\n\n---\n\n4. ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW:\nComponents:\n| Component | Responsibility | Technology | Owned By |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Component 1] | [What it does] | [Tech] | [Team/Role] |\n| [Component 2] | [What it does] | [Tech] | [Team/Role] |\n\nInteraction diagram (text):\n[Component A] ──→ [Component B] : [What is passed]\n[Component B] ──→ [Component C] : [What is passed]\n[Component C] ──→ [Data Store] : [Read/Write — what data]\n\n---\n\n5. DATA DESIGN:\nData Models:\n| Entity | Key Fields | Storage | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Entity] | [Fields] | [e.g., PostgreSQL / Redis / S3] | [Notes] |\n\nData Flow:\n  [Source] → [Transform / Process] → [Destination]\n\nData Retention: [How long data is kept and why]\nSensitive Data: [How PII or sensitive fields are handled]\n\n---\n\n6. API AND INTEGRATION DESIGN:\nInternal APIs:\n| Endpoint | Method | Purpose | Consumer |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [/path] | GET/POST/PUT/DELETE | [Purpose] | [Component/Team] |\n\nExternal Integrations:\n| System | Integration Type | Direction | Failure Handling |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [System] | REST / Webhook / SDK | Inbound / Outbound / Both | [e.g., Retry + circuit breaker] |\n\n---\n\n7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS:\n| Requirement | Target | How Achieved | Validation Method |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Performance | [e.g., API response <200ms at p95] | [Approach] | [Load test] |\n| Scalability | [e.g., Support 10x current user load] | [Approach] | [Stress test] |\n| Security | [e.g., All data encrypted at rest and in transit] | [Approach] | [Security review] |\n| Availability | [e.g., 99.9% uptime] | [Approach] | [Monitoring + alerting] |\n| Maintainability | [e.g., New engineer productive within 1 day] | [Approach] | [Onboarding test] |\n\n---\n\n8. TECHNICAL RISKS:\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation | Owner |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Risk 1] | High/Med/Low | High/Med/Low | [Specific mitigation] | [Role] |\n| [Risk 2] | High/Med/Low | High/Med/Low | [Specific mitigation] | [Role] |\n\n---\n\n9. IMPLEMENTATION GUIDANCE:\nPhasing:\n| Phase | Scope | Dependencies | Est. Duration | Team |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Phase 1 | [Scope] | [Dependencies] | [Duration] | [Team] |\n| Phase 2 | [Scope] | [Dependencies] | [Duration] | [Team] |\n\nKey engineering decisions to make during implementation:\n  - [Decision 1 — e.g., "Choose pagination strategy before building list endpoints"]\n  - [Decision 2]\n\nCode quality expectations:\n  - [e.g., "Unit test coverage ≥ 80% for all new service classes"]\n  - [e.g., "All PRs require review from at least one senior engineer"]\n\n---\n\n10. OPEN QUESTIONS:\n| Question | Why It Matters | Owner | Decision Needed By |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Question 1] | [Impact on design if not answered] | [Role] | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| [Question 2] | [Impact] | [Role] | [DD/MM/YYYY] |
