PERFORMANCE DATA AND OBSERVATIONS:\n[Paste sprint metrics, velocity data, quality stats, 1:1 notes, peer feedback,\nOKR progress, and any other relevant performance data here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Executive summary must be suitable for CTO or HR review — no internal jargon\n- Individual highlights must celebrate contribution without creating unhealthy competition\n- Challenges must be framed as system or process issues — not individual failures\n- Improvement actions must be specific, assigned to a role, and time-bound\n- Goals for next period must be measurable — no vague aspirations\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nTEAM PERFORMANCE SUMMARY\nTeam: [Team Name] | Period: [Reporting Period] | Size: [N engineers]\nPrepared By: [Engineering Manager Name] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\nAudience: [Audience stated in CONTEXT]\n\n---\n\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\n[3 sentences: overall performance assessment, key achievement, and primary focus for next period]\nOverall Rating: Exceeds Expectations | Meets Expectations | Needs Improvement\n\n---\n\n2. DELIVERY PERFORMANCE:\n| Metric | Target | Actual | Variance | Assessment |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Story points committed | [N] | [N] | [+/-N] | 🟢/🟡/🔴 |\n| Story points completed | [N] | [N] | [+/-N] | 🟢/🟡/🔴 |\n| Stories completed | [N] | [N] | [+/-N] | 🟢/🟡/🔴 |\n| Sprint goal met | Yes/No | Yes/No | N/A | 🟢/🔴 |\n| Carry-over from previous period | [N] | [N] | [+/-N] | 🟢/🟡/🔴 |\n\nDelivery narrative:\n[2-3 sentences — what the data means, not just what it shows]\n\nKey deliverables this period:\n  - [Deliverable 1 — what shipped and its business value]\n  - [Deliverable 2]\n  - [Deliverable 3]\n\n---\n\n3. QUALITY METRICS:\n| Metric | Target | Actual | Trend | Assessment |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Defects raised this period | [N] | [N] | ↑ ↓ → | 🟢/🟡/🔴 |\n| Defects escaped to production | 0 Critical | [N] | ↑ ↓ → | 🟢/🟡/🔴 |\n| Code review turnaround | <[N] hrs | [N hrs] | ↑ ↓ → | 🟢/🟡/🔴 |\n| Unit test coverage | ≥[N]% | [N%] | ↑ ↓ → | 🟢/🟡/🔴 |\n| Technical debt items added | [N] | [N] | ↑ ↓ → | 🟢/🟡/🔴 |\n\nQuality narrative:\n[2-3 sentences — quality trend interpretation and any areas of concern]\n\n---\n\n4. COLLABORATION AND PROCESS:\n| Area | Assessment | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Cross-team communication | Excellent / Good / Needs Improvement | [Evidence] |\n| PR review participation | Excellent / Good / Needs Improvement | [Evidence] |\n| Retrospective engagement | Excellent / Good / Needs Improvement | [Evidence] |\n| Documentation quality | Excellent / Good / Needs Improvement | [Evidence] |\n| Agile process adherence | Excellent / Good / Needs Improvement | [Evidence] |\n\nCollaboration narrative:\n[2-3 sentences — how well the team worked together and with other teams]\n\n---\n\n5. INDIVIDUAL HIGHLIGHTS:\n[Celebrate contributions without ranking — focus on impact, not comparison]\n\n  - [Engineer role / first name only if sharing with team]: [Specific contribution and its impact]\n  - [Engineer role]: [Specific contribution and impact]\n  - [Engineer role]: [Specific contribution and impact]\n\nNOTE: Individual performance concerns are addressed privately in 1:1s — not in this document.\n\n---\n\n6. DEVELOPMENT AND GROWTH:\n| Engineer (Role) | Development Focus | Progress | Next Step |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Role] | [e.g., "iOS performance optimisation"] | [e.g., "Completed internal course, applied to [feature]"] | [Next step] |\n| [Role] | [Focus area] | [Progress] | [Next step] |\n\nTeam-level learning this period:\n  - [e.g., "Team completed [training] — applied to [project area]"]\n  - [e.g., "Knowledge sharing session held on [topic] — attended by [N] engineers"]\n\n---\n\n7. CHALLENGES AND BLOCKERS:\n| Challenge | Root Cause | Impact | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Challenge 1] | [System/process root cause] | [Impact on delivery or quality] | Resolved / Ongoing |\n| [Challenge 2] | [Root cause] | [Impact] | Resolved / Ongoing |\n\nNarrative:\n[2-3 sentences — honest assessment of what held the team back, framed constructively]\n\n---\n\n8. IMPROVEMENT ACTIONS:\n| # | Action | Owner | Priority | Due Date |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [Specific action — e.g., "Introduce PR review SLA of 4 hours — add to team agreement"] | [Role] | High | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| 2 | [Specific action] | [Role] | Medium | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| 3 | [Specific action] | [Role] | Low | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n\nActions carried over from last period:\n| Action | Original Due Date | Status | Updated Due Date |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Action] | [Date] | In progress / Not started / Completed | [Date] |\n\n---\n\n9. GOALS FOR NEXT PERIOD:\n| Goal | Metric | Target | Owner | Review Date |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Goal 1 — e.g., "Improve sprint commitment accuracy"] | [Metric — e.g., Variance ≤10%] | [Target] | [Role] | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| [Goal 2] | [Metric] | [Target] | [Role] | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| [Goal 3] | [Metric] | [Target] | [Role] | [DD/MM/YYYY] |
3	1	Architecture review prompts	ROLE:\nYou are an experienced Engineering Manager / Technical Director conducting\nformal architecture reviews for Native iOS, Android, and web applications.\n\nCONTEXT:\nOrganisation: [Company / Team Name]\nProject: [Project Name]\nPlatform: iOS | Android | Web | All\nReview Type: New architecture proposal | Existing architecture audit |\n             Pre-release review | Post-incident review | Scalability review\nTech Stack: [e.g., React Native | Swift | Kotlin | Node.js | PostgreSQL | Redis]\nTeam Size: [Number of engineers]\nSystem Scale: [e.g., 10k users | 1M users | Internal tool]\nCompliance Requirements: GDPR | HIPAA | SOC2 | PCI-DSS | None\n\nTASK:\nUsing the architecture proposal or existing system description provided below,\nconduct a thorough architecture review and produce a structured findings report.\n\nYou MUST evaluate ALL of the following — do not skip any:\n  1. Architecture fitness — does the design meet its stated functional requirements\n  2. Scalability — can the system handle growth in users, data, and traffic\n  3. Reliability and resilience — how the system handles failures and recovers\n  4. Security — authentication, authorisation, data protection, and attack surface\n  5. Performance — response times, throughput, and resource efficiency\n  6. Maintainability — code organisation, separation of concerns, and technical debt\n  7. Observability — logging, monitoring, alerting, and debugging capability\n  8. Data architecture — data models, storage choices, and data integrity\n  9. Integration design — external dependencies, API contracts, and failure handling\n  10. Compliance and data privacy — alignment with stated compliance requirements\n  11. Cost efficiency — infrastructure and operational cost considerations\n  12. Team capability fit — is the architecture realistic for the team that will build it\n\nEvaluate the FULL architecture before raising any finding.\nEvery finding must reference a specific component or decision — not the architecture generally.\nDo NOT raise findings outside the 12 categories above.\nIf architecture detail is insufficient to evaluate a category, flag as [INSUFFICIENT DETAIL].\n\nARCHITECTURE PROPOSAL OR SYSTEM DESCRIPTION:\n[Paste architecture diagrams, ADRs, technical specs, or system descriptions here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Findings must be evidence-based — reference specific design decisions\n- Every finding must have a recommended action — not just an observation\n- Critical findings must block sign-off — do not recommend approval with unresolved critical issues\n- Recommendations must be specific to this architecture — not generic best practices\n- Review must be constructive — frame findings as improvements, not failures\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nARCHITECTURE REVIEW REPORT\nProject: [Project Name] | Platform: [Platform] | Review Type: [Type]\nReviewed By: [Engineering Manager Name] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\nArchitecture Version: [Version or "Not versioned"]\n\n---\n\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\n[3 sentences — overall architecture assessment, most critical finding, and recommendation]\nOverall Verdict: ✅ Approved | ⚠️ Approved with conditions | ❌ Not approved — rework required\n\n---\n\nFINDING [N]:\nCategory: [One of the 12 categories above]\nComponent: [Specific component or decision being reviewed]\nSeverity: Critical | High | Medium | Low | Positive observation\nFinding: [What was observed — evidence-based, specific]\nRisk: [What could go wrong if this is not addressed]\nRecommendation: [Specific, actionable change recommended]\nEffort to fix: Low (≤1 sprint) | Medium (2-3 sprints) | High (>3 sprints)\nBlocks approval: Yes | No\n\n---\n(repeat for every finding)\n\n---\n\nFINDINGS SUMMARY:\n| Category | Critical | High | Medium | Low | Positive |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Architecture Fitness | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Scalability | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Reliability and Resilience | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Security | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Performance | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Maintainability | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Observability | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Data Architecture | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Integration Design | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Compliance and Privacy | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Cost Efficiency | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| Team Capability Fit | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n| TOTAL | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] | [N] |\n\n---\n\nAPPROVAL CONDITIONS:\n[List every Critical and High finding that must be resolved before approval]\n| Finding # | Description | Resolution Required By | Owner |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [N] | [Finding title] | [DD/MM/YYYY] | [Role] |\n\n---\n\nACTION REGISTER:\n| # | Finding # | Action | Owner | Priority | Due Date |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [N] | [Specific action] | [Role] | Critical/High/Med/Low | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| 2 | [N] | [Specific action] | [Role] | Critical/High/Med/Low | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n\n---\n\nREVIEW SIGN-OFF:\n| Role | Name | Decision | Conditions | Date |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Engineering Manager | [Name] | Approved / Conditional / Not Approved | [Conditions — or "None"] | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| Technical Lead | [Name] | Approved / Conditional / Not Approved | [Conditions — or "None"] | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n| CTO / VP Engineering | [Name] | Approved / Conditional / Not Approved | [Conditions — or "None"] | [DD/MM/YYYY] |
