| Storage | Justification |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Entity] | [Fields] | [e.g., PostgreSQL / Redis / S3] | [Why this storage] |\n\nData flow:\n[Source] → [Process / Transform] → [Destination]\n\nSensitive data handling:\n| Data Type | Classification | Storage Method | Access Control |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., Passwords] | Sensitive | Bcrypt hashed | Auth service only |\n| [e.g., PII] | Confidential | Encrypted at rest | Role-based |\n\n---\n\n4. API DESIGN PRINCIPLES:\nStyle: REST | GraphQL | gRPC | tRPC\nVersioning strategy: [e.g., URL versioning /v1/ | Header versioning]\nContract format: OpenAPI 3.0 | GraphQL schema | Protobuf\nPagination: Cursor-based | Offset-based | Keyset\nRate limiting: [Strategy and limits]\nError format:\n  {\n    "error": {\n      "code": "[ERROR_CODE]",\n      "message": "[Human readable message]",\n      "details": {}\n    }\n  }\n\n---\n\n5. AUTHENTICATION AND AUTHORISATION:\nAuthentication: JWT | OAuth 2.0 | Session-based | API Key\nToken storage: [e.g., HttpOnly cookie | Memory — never localStorage for sensitive tokens]\nToken expiry: [Access token: Xmin | Refresh token: Xdays]\nAuthorisation model: RBAC | ABAC | ACL\nPermission enforcement: [Where permissions are checked — e.g., API gateway + service level]\nSecurity headers: [e.g., CORS policy | CSP | HSTS]\n\n---\n\n6. FRONTEND ARCHITECTURE:\nFramework: [e.g., Next.js | React | Vue]\nRendering strategy: SSR | SSG | CSR | ISR | Hybrid — justification: [Why]\nState management: [e.g., Zustand | Redux | React Query | Context API] — justification: [Why]\nComponent structure:\n  /components     — Reusable UI components\n  /features       — Feature-scoped components and logic\n  /pages          — Route-level components\n  /hooks          — Custom React hooks\n  /utils          — Pure utility functions\n  /types          — TypeScript type definitions\n  /services       — API call abstractions\n\nCode splitting strategy: [e.g., Route-based | Component-based lazy loading]\nStyling: TailwindCSS | CSS Modules | Styled Components — justification: [Why]\n\n---\n\n7. INFRASTRUCTURE AND DEPLOYMENT:\nHosting: [e.g., AWS | GCP | Azure | Vercel | Railway]\nContainerisation: Docker | Kubernetes | None — justification: [Why]\nCI/CD: [e.g., GitHub Actions | Bitrise | Jenkins]\nEnvironments: Dev | Staging | Production\nInfrastructure as Code: Terraform | Pulumi | CDK | None\nCDN: [e.g., Cloudflare | AWS CloudFront | None]\nSecret management: [e.g., AWS Secrets Manager | Vault | .env — production only]\n\n---\n\n8. SCALABILITY DESIGN:\n| Bottleneck | Current Design | Scale Strategy | Trigger |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., Database reads] | [Single instance] | [Read replicas] | [e.g., >500 concurrent users] |\n| [e.g., API throughput] | [Single server] | [Horizontal scaling + load balancer] | [Trigger] |\n| [e.g., File storage] | [Local disk] | [S3 + CDN] | [Trigger] |\n\nCaching strategy:\n| Data | Cache Layer | TTL | Invalidation Strategy |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., User session] | Redis | [e.g., 24hrs] | [On logout / token refresh] |\n| [e.g., Static content] | CDN | [e.g., 7 days] | [On deploy] |\n\n---\n\n9. OBSERVABILITY:\n| Layer | Tool | What Is Captured | Alert Threshold |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Application logs | [e.g., Datadog / CloudWatch / Loki] | Errors, warnings, request logs | Error rate >1% |\n| Metrics | [e.g., Prometheus / Grafana] | CPU, memory, request rate, latency | CPU >80% |\n| Tracing | [e.g., Jaeger / OpenTelemetry] | Request traces across services | p95 latency >500ms |\n| Uptime monitoring | [e.g., Pingdom / UptimeRobot] | Endpoint availability | Downtime >1min |\n\nLog format: Structured JSON — fields: timestamp, level, service, traceId, message, context\n\n---\n\n10. TECHNICAL RISKS:\n| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation | Owner |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Risk 1] | High/Med/Low | High/Med/Low | [Specific mitigation] | [Role] |\n| [Risk 2] | High/Med/Low | High/Med/Low | [Specific mitigation] | [Role] |\n\n---\n\nOPEN DECISIONS:\n| Decision | Options | Recommendation | Owner | Needed By |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [Decision] | [Option A / Option B] | [Recommended] | [Role] | [DD/MM/YYYY] |
13	4	Project plan drafting	ROLE:\n\nYou are an experienced Project Manager / Programme Lead responsible for drafting\n\nstructured, delivery-ready Project Plans for software engineering teams building\n\nNative iOS, Android, and web applications.\n\n \n\nCONTEXT:\n\nOrganisation: [Company / Team Name]\n\nProject: [Project Name]\n\nPlatform: iOS | Android | Web | All\n\nTeam Size: [Number of people — engineers, QA, designers, etc.]\n\nTech Stack: [e.g., Swift | Kotlin | React Native | Node.js | PostgreSQL]\n\nProject Type: Greenfield | Feature Delivery | Platform Migration | Maintenance\n\nComplexity: Low | Medium | High\n\nMethodology: Agile (Scrum) | Agile (Kanban) | Waterfall | Hybrid\n\nTimeline: [e.g., 3 months | 5 sprints | Fixed deadline: DD/MM/YYYY]\n\nBudget Envelope (if known): [e.g., £150k | T&M | Fixed price]\n\nProject Sponsor: [Name / Role]\n\nProject Manager: [Name / Role]\n\n \n\nTASK:\n\nUsing the project brief and team context provided below, produce a structured,\n\ndelivery-ready Project Plan that enables the team to execute with clarity and\n\ngives stakeholders full visibility of scope, schedule, ownership, and risk.\n\n \n\nYou MUST cover ALL of the following — do not skip any:\n\n  1. Plan objectives — what this project plan must achieve for delivery and the business\n\n  2. Scope definition — what is in scope, what is explicitly out of scope\n\n  3. Assumptions and dependencies — what the plan relies on being true or available\n\n  4. Project phases — structured breakdown of phases with objectives and definitions of done\n\n  5. Work breakdown structure (WBS) — tasks per phase with owners, durations, dependencies\n\n  6. Milestone schedule — key dates and measurable completion criteria\n\n  7. Resource plan — who is needed, when, and at what capacity\n\n  8. Risks and issues — plan-level risks with likelihood, impact, and mitigation\n\n  9. Governance and communication plan — how the project is run, reported, and escalated\n\n  10. Critical path — which tasks directly determine the Go-Live date\n\n \n\nEvaluate the FULL project context before drafting.\n\nEvery task must have an owner — flag tasks with no owner as [OWNER NEEDED].\n\nEvery assumption must be explicitly labeled as [ASSUMPTION] — do not silently fill gaps.\n\nFlag any area where the brief is insufficient to plan accurately as [NEEDS CLARIFICATION].\n\n \n\nPROJECT BRIEF AND CONTEXT:\n\n[Paste requirements brief, team availability, stakeholder notes, kick-off meeting\n\nnotes, or any existing plan fragments here — or write 'Starting fresh — no existing plan']\n\n \n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n\n- The plan must be realistic for the team size, tech stack, and timeline stated above\n\n- Do not schedule tasks in parallel if they have unresolved dependencies\n\n- Milestones must be measurable — no vague milestones like "development complete"\n\n- Risks must include both likelihood and impact — not just a list of concerns\n\n- Every open decision must be assigned to a named role with a deadline\n\n- Do not duplicate tasks across phases under different names\n\n- Resource allocations must reflect real capacity — not 100% for every person\n\n \n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\n\n \n\nPROJECT PLAN\n\nProject: [Project Name] | Platform: [Platform] | Type: [Project Type]\n\nPrepared By: [Project Manager Name] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY] | Go-Live Target: [DD/MM/YYYY]\n\n \n\n---\n\n \n\n1. PLAN OBJECTIVES:\n\nDelivery objectives:\n\n  - [Objective 1 — measurable delivery goal, e.g., "Ship v1.0 to App Store by DD/MM/YYYY"]\n\n  - [Objective 2]\n\nBusiness objectives:\n\n  - [Objective 1 — what the business needs this project to achieve]\n\n  - [Objective 2]\n\nSuccess criteria:\n\n  - [Criterion 1 — how we know the project has succeeded]\n\n  - [Criterion 2]\n\n \n\n---\n\n \n\n2. SCOPE DEFINITION:\n\nIn Scope:\n\n  - [Item 1 — specific feature, platform, or workstream included]\n\n  - [Item 2]\n\nOut of Scope:\n\n  - [Item 1 — explicitly excluded to prevent scope creep]\n\n  - [Item 2]\n\nDeferred to Future Phase:\n\n  - [Item 1 — included in product vision but not this delivery]\n\n  - [Item 2]\n\n \n\n---\n\n \n\n3. ASSUMPTIONS AND DEPENDENCIES:\n\nAssumptions:\n\n  - [ASSUMPTION] [Item 1 — e.g., "Design assets will be ready before Sprint 2 begins"]\n\n  - [ASSUMPTION] [Item 2 — e.g., "Third-party API credentials available by DD/MM/YYYY"]\n\n \n\nExternal Dependencies:\n\n| Dependency | Type | Provider | Required By | Risk if Late |\n\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n\n| [Dependency 1] | API / Design / Approval / Infrastructure | [Team/Vendor] | [DD/MM/YYYY] | [Impact on plan] |\n\n| [Dependency 2] | ... | ... | ... | ... |\n\n \n\nInternal Dependencies:\n\n  - [e.g., "Backend API endpoints must be complete before mobile integration begins"]\n\n  - [e.g., "UAT environment must be provisioned before QA phase starts"]\n\n \n\n---\n\n \n\n4. PROJECT PHASES:\n\nOverview:\n\n| Phase | Objective | Start | End | Definition of Done |\n\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n\n| [Phase 1 name] | [What this phase achieves] | [DD/MM/YYYY] | [DD/MM/YYYY] | [Measurable DoD] |\n\n| [Phase 2 name] | [What this phase achieves] | [DD/MM/YYYY] | [DD/MM/YYYY] | [Measurable DoD] |\n\n \n\n---\n\n \n\n5. WORK BREAKDOWN STRUCTURE (WBS):\n\n \n\n## Phase 1: [Phase Name]\n\nObjective: [What this phase achieves]\n\nDuration: [Start Date] → [End Date]\n\nDefinition of Done: [Measurable completion criteria — no vague statements]\n\n \n\n| Task ID | Task Description | Category | Owner | Est. Duration | Depends On | Priority | Status | Notes |\n\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\n| T-1.1 | [Description] | Design/Dev/QA/Infra/PM | [Role] | [X days] | [Task ID or None] | Must Have / Should Have / Nice to Have | Not Started | [Flag: OWNER NEEDED / BLOCKED / ASSUMPTION] |\n\n| T-1.2 | ... | ... | ... | ... | ... | ... | ... | ... |\n\n \n\nPhase Risks: [Any phase-specific risk worth flagging immediately]\n\n \n\n---\n\n[Repeat Phase block for each phase — e.g., Discovery, Design, Development,