ion based on assumption as [ASSUMPTION].\n\nINFRASTRUCTURE REQUIREMENTS:\n[Paste architecture diagram description, existing setup details, team constraints,\ncompliance requirements, or existing IaC fragments here —\nor "Greenfield — no existing infrastructure"]\n\nSPECIAL REQUIREMENTS:\n[Any compliance needs — e.g., GDPR, HIPAA, PCI-DSS | Multi-region | DR requirements]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Never hardcode credentials, passwords, API keys, or account IDs\n- All secrets must be referenced from a secrets manager — not from variables files\n- Every resource must have environment and project tags — no untagged resources\n- IAM policies must follow least-privilege principle — no wildcard permissions\n  unless explicitly justified\n- Production and non-production environments must be fully isolated\n- All storage must have encryption at rest enabled\n- All data in transit must use TLS 1.2 minimum\n- IaC must be idempotent — safe to apply multiple times without side effects\n- Destruction protection must be enabled for production stateful resources\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\n\nINFRASTRUCTURE AS CODE\nProject: [Project Name] | Tool: [IaC Tool] | Provider: [Cloud Provider]\nEnvironment: [Environment] | Prepared By: [Engineer Role] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\n\n---\n\n1. PROJECT STRUCTURE:\n[Recommended directory and file structure for this IaC project]\n\n[Project Root]/\n  - modules/\n    - networking/\n    - compute/\n    - database/\n    - storage/\n  - environments/\n    - dev/\n    - staging/\n    - production/\n  - main.tf / index.ts / app.py\n  - variables.tf\n  - outputs.tf\n  - backend.tf\n\n---\n\n2. VARIABLES AND CONFIGURATION:\n[All input variables with descriptions, types, defaults, and validation rules]\n\n[CONFIG: PROJECT_NAME] — Project identifier used in all resource names and tags\n[CONFIG: ENVIRONMENT] — Target environment: dev | staging | production\n[CONFIG: AWS_REGION] — Primary deployment region\n[CONFIG: DB_INSTANCE_CLASS] — Database instance size per environment\n[CONFIG: MIN_CAPACITY] — Minimum number of compute instances\n[CONFIG: MAX_CAPACITY] — Maximum number of compute instances\n\nEnvironment-Specific Values:\n| Variable | Dev | Staging | Production |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., Instance Type] | [e.g., t3.small] | [e.g., t3.medium] | [e.g., t3.large] |\n| [e.g., DB Instance] | [e.g., db.t3.micro] | [e.g., db.t3.small] | [e.g., db.r6g.large] |\n| [e.g., Min Instances] | [e.g., 1] | [e.g., 2] | [e.g., 3] |\n| [e.g., Multi-AZ DB] | [e.g., false] | [e.g., false] | [e.g., true] |\n\n---\n\n3. STATE MANAGEMENT:\n[Remote state backend configuration]\n\n# [REPLACE: S3_BUCKET_NAME] — Create this bucket manually before first apply\n# [REPLACE: DYNAMODB_TABLE_NAME] — Create this table manually before first apply\n# [CONFIG: AWS_REGION] — Must match primary deployment region\n\n[Complete backend configuration code block here]\n\nState Locking: Enabled | Disabled — [tool used]\nState Encryption: Yes | No\nWorkspace Strategy: [e.g., One workspace per environment | Separate state files]\n\n---\n\n4. NETWORK LAYER:\n[Complete networking configuration — VPC, subnets, routing, security groups]\n\n# VPC Configuration\n# [ASSUMPTION] CIDR ranges below assume no overlap with existing networks\n# [NEEDS CLARIFICATION] if VPC peering with existing infrastructure is required\n\n[Complete VPC and subnet configuration code block here]\n\n# Security Groups\n# Principle: default-deny — only explicitly required traffic permitted\n\n[Complete security group configuration code block here]\n\nNetwork Architecture Summary:\n| Component | CIDR / Value | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., VPC] | [CONFIG: VPC_CIDR] | [e.g., Primary network boundary] |\n| [e.g., Public Subnet AZ-A] | [CONFIG: PUBLIC_SUBNET_1_CIDR] | [e.g., Load balancer, NAT Gateway] |\n| [e.g., Private Subnet AZ-A] | [CONFIG: PRIVATE_SUBNET_1_CIDR] | [e.g., Application layer] |\n| [e.g., DB Subnet AZ-A] | [CONFIG: DB_SUBNET_1_CIDR] | [e.g., Database layer — no internet access] |\n\n---\n\n5