ructure detail is missing, flag it as [NEEDS DECISION] — never assume.\n\nPROJECT INFRASTRUCTURE REQUIREMENTS:\n[Paste current infrastructure state, constraints, budget limits, and requirements here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- All infrastructure components must be reproducible via code — no manual click-ops setup\n- Local setup instructions must work on macOS and Linux — call out Windows exceptions explicitly\n- Container images must be pinned to specific versions — never use "latest" tag\n- Device farm costs must be considered — do not recommend premium tiers without justification\n- Every configuration file produced must be valid, ready-to-use syntax — no pseudocode\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nAUTOMATION INFRASTRUCTURE SETUP PLAN\nProject: [Project Name] | Platform: [Platform] | Infrastructure: [Local/Cloud/Hybrid]\nPrepared By: [Name] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\n\n---\n\n1. INFRASTRUCTURE ARCHITECTURE:\n[ASCII or text diagram showing all components and their connections]\n\nComponents:\n| Component | Purpose | Technology | Hosted On |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Test Runner | Executes automation suite | [e.g., Appium Server] | [Local / CI agent / Docker] |\n| Device Provider | Supplies test devices | [e.g., AVD / BrowserStack] | [Local / Cloud] |\n| Artifact Storage | Stores reports and binaries | [e.g., S3 / CI artifacts] | [Cloud] |\n| [Additional component] | [Purpose] | [Technology] | [Location] |\n\n---\n\n2. LOCAL DEVELOPMENT SETUP:\nPrerequisites:\n| Tool | Version | macOS Install | Linux Install | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., Node.js] | [e.g., 20.x LTS] | brew install node | apt install nodejs | [Purpose] |\n| [e.g., Appium] | [e.g., 2.x] | npm install -g appium | npm install -g appium | [Purpose] |\n| [e.g., Android Studio] | [e.g., Latest stable] | [Download link] | [Download link] | AVD management |\n\nFirst-run setup steps:\n  1. [Step]\n  2. [Step]\n  3. [Step]\n  ...\n  N. Run: [Exact command to execute first test and confirm setup is working]\n\n---\n\n3. CI/CD INFRASTRUCTURE:\n| Agent / Runner | OS | CPU | RAM | Storage | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., GitHub-hosted runner] | [e.g., macOS 14] | [e.g., 3-core] | [e.g., 14GB] | [e.g., 14GB SSD] | iOS test execution |\n| [e.g., Self-hosted runner] | [e.g., Ubuntu 22.04] | [e.g., 4-core] | [e.g., 16GB] | [e.g., 50GB SSD] | Android test execution |\n\nSizing Justification: [Why these specs — based on suite size and parallel job count]\n\n---\n\n4. DEVICE AND BROWSER PROVISIONING:\niOS:\n  Type: Simulator | Real Device | Device Farm\n  Config: [e.g., iPhone 15 Pro — iOS 17.4 — Xcode 15]\n  Provisioning Command: [Exact command to start simulator]\n\nAndroid:\n  Type: Emulator | Real Device | Device Farm\n  Config: [e.g., Pixel 7 API 34 — Android 14]\n  Provisioning Command: [Exact command to start emulator]\n\nDevice Farm (if applicable):\n  Provider: [Provider name]\n  Integration Method: [SDK / REST API / CLI]\n  Config: [Ready-to-use connection config]\n\n---\n\n5. CONTAINERISATION STRATEGY:\n[Skip this section with a note if containerisation is "None" in CONTEXT]\n\nDockerfile: [Ready-to-use Dockerfile for the test runner — pinned versions, no "latest"]\nDocker Compose: [Ready-to-use docker-compose.yml if multiple services are needed]\nKubernetes: [Helm chart or manifest if Kubernetes is in scope — or "Not in scope"]\n\n---\n\n6. ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION MANAGEMENT:\n| Config Item | Dev | QA | Staging | Storage Method |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| App endpoint URL | [Value] | [Value] | [Value] | Environment variable |\n| Device UDID | [Value] | [Value] | [Value] | CI secret |\n| Test user credentials | [Value] | [Value] | [Value] | Secrets manager |\n\nSwitching Mechanism: [How environment is selected at runtime — e.g., ENV=qa make test]\n\n---\n\n7. NETWORK AND PROXY CONFIGURATION:\nCorporate Proxy: [Proxy settings if applicable — or "Not required"]\nVPN Requirements: [Any VPN needed to reach test environments — or "None"]\nFirewall Rules: [Ports and endpoints