current quality pain points, and specific improvement goals here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Every metric must have a precise mathematical definition — not a narrative description\n- Targets must be specific and time-bound — not "improve over time"\n- Data collection method must be automated where possible — manual collection is a risk\n- Dashboard must be tailored per audience — executives do not need the same view as engineers\n- Anti-patterns section must call out any metric in this framework that could become a vanity metric if misused\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nQUALITY METRICS FRAMEWORK\nProgramme: [Name] | Platform: [Platform] | Version: [X.X]\nPrepared By: [Test Architect Name] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY] | Review Cycle: [e.g., Quarterly]\n\n---\n\n1. METRICS SELECTION:\n| Metric | Category | Improvement Goal Supported | Justification for Inclusion |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Metric name] | [e.g., Coverage / Defect / Efficiency] | [Goal it supports] | [Why this metric matters here] |\n\n---\n\n2. METRIC DEFINITIONS:\nMETRIC: [Metric Name]\nCategory: Coverage | Defect | Efficiency | Automation | Process\nDefinition: [Plain English definition — one sentence]\nFormula: [Metric Name] = [Numerator] / [Denominator] x 100\nExample: [Worked example with real numbers]\nMeasured At: [e.g., End of each sprint | Per release | Daily]\nData Source: [e.g., JIRA defect count | TestRail execution results | CI pipeline]\nCollection Method: Automated | Manual | Semi-automated\nOwner: [Role responsible for this metric]\n\n---\n(repeat for every metric)\n\n---\n\n3. BASELINE AND TARGETS:\n| Metric | Current Baseline | Target | Target Date | Measurement Frequency |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Test Coverage | [N% — or NEEDS BASELINE CAPTURE] | 100% of AC | [Date] | Per sprint |\n| Automation Coverage | [N% — or NEEDS BASELINE CAPTURE] | [N]% | [Date] | Monthly |\n| Defect Escape Rate | [N — or NEEDS BASELINE CAPTURE] | 0 Critical | Per release | Per release |\n| Pass Rate | [N% — or NEEDS BASELINE CAPTURE] | ≥95% | [Date] | Per sprint |\n| Mean Time to Detect | [N days — or NEEDS BASELINE CAPTURE] | <[N] hours | [Date] | Monthly |\n| Flaky Test Rate | [N% — or NEEDS BASELINE CAPTURE] | <2% | [Date] | Weekly |\n| [Additional metric] | | | | |\n\n---\n\n4. DATA COLLECTION:\n| Metric | Data Source | Collection Method | Frequency | Automated? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Test Coverage | TestRail / JIRA | Export via API | Per sprint | Yes |\n| Automation Coverage | CI pipeline report | Script parses results | Per run | Yes |\n| Defect Escape Rate | JIRA — production bugs label | JIRA filter + API | Per release | Yes |\n| Pass Rate | CI pipeline / TestRail | Automated report | Per run | Yes |\n| Mean Time to Detect | JIRA created date vs commit timestamp | Script calculation | Monthly | Semi |\n| Flaky Test Rate | CI pipeline flaky test flag | Automated tagging | Per run | Yes |\n\n---\n\n5. REPORTING CADENCE:\n| Metric | Engineering Team | QA Lead | Product | Executive |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Test Coverage | Per sprint | Per sprint | Per release | Per quarter |\n| Automation Coverage | Monthly | Monthly | Per quarter | Per quarter |\n| Defect Escape Rate | Per release | Per release | Per release | Per release |\n| Pass Rate | Per run | Per sprint | Per release | Per release |\n| Mean Time to Detect | Monthly | Monthly | Per quarter | Per quarter |\n| Flaky Test Rate | Weekly | Weekly | — | — |\n\n---\n\n6. DASHBOARD DESIGN:\nENGINEERING TEAM DASHBOARD:\nPurpose: Day-to-day visibility of test health and pipeline status\nMetrics Shown: Pass rate, flaky test rate, automation coverage, open defects by severity\nFormat: Live CI dashboard | JIRA board | [Tool]\nRefresh Rate: Real-time | Per run\n\nQA LEAD DASHBOARD:\nPurpose: Sprint and release quality tracking\nMetrics Shown: All engineering metrics + test coverage, defect escape rate, mean time to detect\nFormat: TestRail report | JIRA dashboard | [Tool]\nRefresh Rate: Daily\n\nPRODUCT DASHBOARD:\nPurpose: Release readiness and quality trend visibility\nMetrics Shown: Pass rate trend, defect escape rate, release sign-off status\nFormat: Confluence page | Custom report | [Tool]\nRefresh Rate: Per sprint / Per release\n\nEXECUTIVE DASHBOARD:\nPurpose: Programme-level quality health and trend\nMetrics Shown: Defect escape rate trend, automation ROI, release quality score\nFormat: Single-page summary | Slide deck | [Tool]\nRefresh Rate: Monthly / Per quarter\n\n---\n\n7. METRICS ANTI-PATTERNS:\n| Anti-Pattern | Why It Is Harmful | Safe Alternative |\n|---|---|---|\n| Test case count as a quality measure | More tests ≠ better quality — encourages padding | Use test coverage against AC instead |\n| 100% pass rate as success | May indicate insufficient test challenge, not quality | Track pass rate alongside defect escape rate |\n| Defect count as team performance KPI | Discourages defect reporting — hides quality problems | Use defect escape rate and time to detect instead |\n| Automation percentage without ROI | High automation % means nothing if tests are flaky or irrelevant | Pair automation coverage with flaky test rate and maintenance cost |\n| [Additional anti-pattern] | [Why harmful] | [Safe alternative] |\n\n---\n\n8. METRICS EVOLUTION:\n| Programme Stage | Active Metrics | Retire | Add |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Project kickoff | Coverage, pass rate, defect count | — | — |\n| Mid-programme | All above + automation coverage, flaky rate | Defect count (replace with escape rate) | Mean time to detect |\n| Pre-release | All above + escape rate, release readiness score | — | Release quality score |\n| BAU / Scaled | Stable set + automation ROI | Sprint-level coverage (replace with trend) | Cost of quality |\n\n---\n\nBASELINES NEEDING CAPTURE:\n| Metric | Action | Owner | By Date |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Any NEEDS BASELINE CAPTURE items] | Instrument data collection | [Role] | [DD/MM/YYYY] |
51	14	Troubleshooting guides	ROLE:\nYou are a senior Technical Support Specialist (L2/L3) responsible for producing\nstructured troubleshooting guides for Native iOS, Android, and web applications.\n\nCONTEXT:\nProject / Product: [Product Name]\nPlatform: iOS | Android | Web | All\nSupport Tier: L1 — Basic user guidance | L2 — Technical investigation | L3 — Engineering escalation\nAudience: L1 Support Agent | End User | Internal Engineering | All\nIssue Category: Authentication | Performance | Crash | Data sync | Network |\n               Installation | Feature malfunction | [Other]\nApp Version: [Version — or "All versions"]\nEnvironment: Production | Staging | All\n\nTASK:\nUsing the issue description and known symptoms provided below, produce a complete\ntroubleshooting guide that enables the stated audience to diagnose and resolve the issue\nwithout escalation where possible.\n\nYou MUST cover ALL of the following — do not skip any:\n  1. Issue overview — clear, jargon-free description of the problem and its user impact\n  2. Symptom identification — how to confirm this is the correct guide for the reported issue\n  3. Pre-investigation checklist — information to gather before starting diagnosis\n  4. Diagnostic steps — ordered, tiered steps from simplest to most complex\n  5. Resolution actions — specific fix for each identified root cause\n  6. Escalation criteria — exact conditions that require escalation to next tier\n  7. Escalation package — what information must be collected before escalating\n  8. Prevention — steps to prevent recurrence or detect early\n\nEvaluate the FULL issue description before writing any diagnostic step.\nSteps must be ordered from least disruptive to most disruptive — never start with destructive actions.\nEvery diagnostic step must state what a positive and negative result means.\nDo NOT include steps that require access or permissions beyond the stated support tier.\n\nISSUE DESCRIPTION AND KNOWN SYMPTOMS:\n[Paste issue description, error messages, affected user reports, and any known context here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Steps must be written so an L1 agent with no engineering background can follow them\n- Every step must be atomic — one action per step, never compound\n- Diagnostic steps must be platform-specific where iOS and Android differ\n- Resolution actions must be tied to a specific diagnosed cause — not generic fixes\n- Escalation criteria must be explicit conditions — not "if unsure, escalate"\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nTROUBLESHOOTING GUIDE\nIssue Title: [Clear, searchable title — what fails + where + on what platform]\nGuide ID: TG-[NNN]\nPlatform: iOS | Android | Web | All\nSupport Tier: L1 | L2 | L3\nVersion: [X.X] | Last Updated: [DD/MM/YYYY]\n\n---\n\n1. ISSUE OVERVIEW:\nDescription: [Plain English — what the user experiences, not the technical cause]\nUser Impact: [e.g., Cannot log in | Data not saving | App crashes on launch]\nAffected Users: [e.g., All users | Users on iOS 17+ | Users with [specific config]]\nFrequency: Common | Intermittent | Rare | Unknown\n\n---\n\n2. SYMPTOM IDENTIFICATION:\nUse this guide if ALL of the following are true:\n  ✅ [Symptom 1 — e.g., "User reports error message: [exact message text]"]\n  ✅ [Symptom 2]\n  ✅ [Symptom 3]\n\nDo NOT use this guide if:\n  ❌ [Condition — e.g., "Error occurs only during checkout — use TG-[NNN] instead"]\n  ❌ [Condition]\n\n---\n\n3. PRE-INVESTIGATION CHECKLIST:\nCollect ALL of the following before starting diagnosis:\n  - [ ] App version number\n  - [ ] Device model and OS version\n  - [ ] Steps the user took before the issue occurred\n  - [ ] Error message text (exact — screenshot if possible)\n  - [ ] Time and frequency of occurrence\n  - [ ] Network type at time of issue (WiFi / Mobile data / VPN)\n  - [ ] [Additional item relevant to this issue]\n\n---\n\n4. DIAGNOSTIC STEPS:\nSTEP 1 — [Step title]\nAction: [Exact action to perform]\nPositive result (issue found): [What it means + go to Resolution A]\nNegative result (not this cause): [What it means + proceed to Step 2]\n\nSTEP 2 — [Step title]\nAction: [Exact action to perform]\nPositive result: [What it means + go to Resolution B]\nNegative result: [What it means + proceed to Step 3]\n\nSTEP 3 — [Step title]\nAction: [Exact action to perform]\nPositive result: [What it means + go to Resolution C]\nNegative result: [What it means + see Escalation Criteria]\n\n---\n(add steps as needed — order from least to most disruptive)\n\n---\n\n5. RESOLUTION ACTIONS:\nRESOLUTION A — [Root cause identified in Step 1]\nSteps:\n  1. [Action]\n  2. [Action]\n  3. [Action]\nExpected outcome: [What the user should see when resolved]\nVerification: [How to confirm the issue is resolved]\nIf unresolved after this: [Next action — or "Escalate per Section 6"]\n\nRESOLUTION B — [Root cause identified in Step 2]\nSteps:\n  1. [Action]\n  2. [Action]\nExpected outcome: [Expected outcome]\nVerification: [Verification step]\nIf unresolved after this: [Next action]\n\n---\n(repeat for every resolution)\n\n---\n\n6. ESCALATION CRITERIA:\nEscalate to [L2 / L3 / Engineering] immediately if ANY of the following are true:\n  🔴 [Condition — e.g., "Issue affects more than 10 users simultaneously"]\n  🔴 [Condition — e.g., "Data loss or corruption is reported"]\n  🔴 [Condition — e.g., "All diagnostic steps completed with no resolution found"]\n  🔴 [Condition — e.g., "Error code [X] appears in logs"]\n\nDo NOT escalate without completing Section 7 first.\n\n---\n\n7. ESCALATION PACKAGE:\nBefore escalating, collect and attach ALL of the following:\n  - [ ] Completed pre-investigation checklist (Section 3)\n  - [ ] Diagnostic steps completed and results of each\n  - [ ] Resolution actions attempted and outcomes\n  - [ ] Device logs / crash report / network trace (if accessible at this tier)\n  - [ ] Screenshots or screen recording of the issue\n  - [ ] Number of affected users and time of first report\n  - [ ] [Additional item specific to this issue]\n\nEscalation template:\n  Issue: [Guide ID] — [Issue Title]\n  Reported by: [User / Ticket ID]\n  Steps completed: [List]\n  Outcome: [What happened]\n  Attachments: [List]\n\n---\n\n8. PREVENTION:\n| Prevention Action | Who | Frequency | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [e.g., Check app version on user login] | Support Agent | Each contact | Catch outdated app versions early |\n| [e.g., Monitor error rate dashboard] | L2 Support | Daily | Detect spikes before user volume escalates |\n| [e.g., Clear cache advisory in onboarding] | Product / L1 | One-time | Reduce cache-related tickets |\n\nKnown Recurrence Triggers:\n  - [e.g., "Issue recurs after app update — re-verify resolution after each release"]\n  - [e.g., "Issue more common on low-storage devices — advise storage check proactively"]\n\nRelated Guides:\n  | Guide ID | Title | When to Use Instead |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | TG-[NNN] | [Title] | [Condition] |
