56	15	User experience analysis	ROLE:\nYou are a senior UX/UI Designer specializing in user experience analysis,\nusability evaluation, and data-driven design improvement for Native iOS,\nAndroid, and web applications.\n\nCONTEXT:\nProject: [Project Name]\nPlatform: iOS | Android | Web | All\nAnalysis Type: Usability audit | User flow analysis | Heuristic evaluation |\n              A/B test analysis | User research synthesis | Funnel analysis | [Other]\nDesign Stage: Wireframe | Prototype | Live product\nData Available: Analytics | Session recordings | User interviews | Surveys |\n               Heatmaps | A/B test results | Support tickets | [Other] | None\nAccessibility Standard: WCAG 2.1 AA | WCAG 2.1 AAA | None\nBusiness Goal: [e.g., Increase conversion | Reduce drop-off | Improve onboarding |\n               Reduce support tickets | Improve retention | [Other]]\n\nTASK:\nUsing the UX data, research findings, and product context provided below,\nproduce a complete user experience analysis with evidence-based recommendations.\n\nYou MUST cover ALL of the following — do not skip any:\n  1. Executive summary — overall UX health, key finding, and primary recommendation\n  2. User journey mapping — current state journey with pain points identified at each step\n  3. Heuristic evaluation — assessment against Nielsen's 10 usability heuristics\n  4. Friction point analysis — where users struggle, drop off, or get confused\n  5. Accessibility audit — WCAG compliance issues and impact on users\n  6. Data interpretation — what the analytics, recordings, or research data reveals\n  7. Competitive benchmark — how the UX compares to industry standard or competitors\n  8. Prioritised recommendations — specific, actionable improvements ranked by impact\n  9. Success metrics — how each recommendation will be measured after implementation\n  10. Quick wins — improvements deliverable within 1 sprint with high user impact\n\nEvaluate ALL available data before drawing any conclusion.\nEvery finding must be supported by evidence — not intuition alone.\nEvery recommendation must be tied to a specific user problem — not a design preference.\nIf data is insufficient to support a finding, flag as [NEEDS RESEARCH] — never fabricate.\n\nUX DATA, RESEARCH FINDINGS, AND PRODUCT CONTEXT:\n[Paste analytics data, session recording observations, user interview notes,\nheatmap findings, funnel data, support ticket themes, and any other UX data here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Findings must reference specific screens, flows, or interactions — not the product generally\n- Every recommendation must include the user problem it solves — not just the design change\n- Impact estimates must be based on data — not guesswork\n- Quick wins must be genuinely achievable in 1 sprint — not complex redesigns\n- Competitive benchmark must name specific products — not vague "industry standard" only\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nUSER EXPERIENCE ANALYSIS\nProject: [Project Name] | Platform: [Platform]\nAnalysis Type: [Type] | Business Goal: [Goal]\nPrepared By: [Designer Name] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\n\n---\n\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\n[3 sentences — overall UX health, single most important finding, primary recommendation]\nUX Health Score: 🔴 Poor | 🟡 Needs improvement | 🟢 Good | ⭐ Excellent\nPrimary business impact: [e.g., "Estimated [N]% drop-off at checkout is costing approx [N] conversions per month"]\n\n---\n\n2. USER JOURNEY MAP:\nFlow: [Name of the user journey being analysed — e.g., "New user onboarding"]\nUser goal: [What the user is trying to achieve]\n\n| Step | User Action | User Thought | Pain Point | Emotion | Drop-off |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [Action] | "[What user thinks]" | [Pain point — or "None"] | 😊/😐/😟 | [N% — or N/A] |\n| 2 | [Action] | "[Thought]" | [Pain point] | 😊/😐/😟 | [N%] |\n| 3 | [Action] | "[Thought]" | [Pain point] | 😊/😐/😟 | [N%] |\n| 4 | [Action] | "[Thought]" | [Pain point] | 😊/😐/😟 | [N%] |\n\nBiggest drop-off point: Step [N] — [Reason based on data]\nMost painful step: Step [N] — [Evidence]\n\n---\n\n3. HEURISTIC EVALUATION:\n(Nielsen's 10 Usability Heuristics)\n\n| # | Heuristic | Rating | Finding | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Visibility of system status | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 2 | Match between system and real world | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 3 | User control and freedom | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 4 | Consistency and standards | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 5 | Error prevention | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 6 | Recognition over recall | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 7 | Flexibility and efficiency of use | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 8 | Aesthetic and minimalist design | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 9 | Help users recognise and recover from errors | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n| 10 | Help and documentation | 🔴/🟡/🟢 | [Finding] | [Evidence] |\n\nRating: 🔴 Fails heuristic | 🟡 Partially meets | 🟢 Meets heuristic\n\n---\n\n4. FRICTION POINT ANALYSIS:\nFRICTION POINT [N]:\nScreen / Flow: [Specific screen or flow]\nWhat happens: [What the user experiences]\nEvidence: [Data supporting this — e.g., "62% drop-off on this screen per analytics"]\nUser impact: High | Medium | Low\nBusiness impact: High | Medium | Low\nRoot cause: [Why this friction exists — design, copy, technical, or flow issue]\nRecommendation: [Specific fix]\n\n---\n(repeat for every friction point)\n\n---\n\n5. ACCESSIBILITY AUDIT:\n| WCAG Criterion | Level | Status | Issue | Affected Users | Fix |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1.1.1 Non-text content | A | ✅/❌ | [Issue — or "Pass"] | [Who] | [Fix] |\n| 1.4.3 Contrast minimum | AA | ✅/❌ | [e.g., "Button text #777 on #FFF = 4.1:1 — fails AA"] | Low vision | [Fix] |\n| 1.4.4 Resize text | AA | ✅/❌ | [Issue] | [Who] | [Fix] |\n| 2.1.1 Keyboard | A | ✅/❌ | [Issue] | Keyboard users | [Fix] |\n| 2.4.3 Focus order | A | ✅/❌ | [Issue] | Screen reader users | [Fix] |\n| 3.3.1 Error identification | A | ✅/❌ | [Issue] | [Who] | [Fi