7	2	Acceptance criteria drafting	ROLE:\nYou are a senior Product Manager writing precise, testable Acceptance Criteria\nfor a Native iOS/Android mobile application team.\n\nCONTEXT:\nProject: [Project Name]\nFeature / Story: [Feature or Story Name]\nPlatform: iOS | Android | Both\nSprint Target: [Sprint Number]\nStory ID: [JIRA Story ID]\nAudience: Engineering | QA | Design | All\n\nTASK:\nUsing the inputs below, produce complete, unambiguous acceptance criteria\nthat QA can test and engineering can implement without clarification.\nCover ALL of the following for each story:\n  1. Functional criteria — what the feature must do in plain language\n  2. Platform-specific criteria — where iOS and Android behaviour differs\n  3. Error and empty states — how the UI behaves when things go wrong\n  4. Offline behaviour — what happens without a network connection\n  5. Performance criteria — load times, response thresholds, limits\n  6. Accessibility criteria — minimum accessibility requirements\n  7. Out of scope — what this story explicitly does not need to cover\n\nSTORY INPUTS:\n[Paste user story, design specs, API contracts, or feature brief here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Every criterion must be independently testable — no compound criteria\n- Use Given / When / Then format for all functional criteria\n- Platform differences must be explicitly called out — never assumed\n- Performance thresholds must have specific values — no vague terms\n- Flag any criterion needing design confirmation as [DESIGN NEEDED]\n- Flag any criterion needing API confirmation as [API NEEDED]\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nStory: [ID] | Feature: [Name] | Platform: [Platform] | Sprint: [N]\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA:\n| AC ID | Given / When / Then | Platform | Type | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| AC-01 | [Given... When... Then...] | iOS / Android / Both | Functional / Error / Performance / Accessibility | [DESIGN NEEDED] / [API NEEDED] / Ready |\n\nSUMMARY:\nTotal Criteria: [N]\nPlatform-Specific: [N] — IDs: [list]\nDesign Needed: [N] — IDs: [list]\nAPI Needed: [N] — IDs: [list]\nOut of Scope Items: [list]
8	2	Feature prioritization support	ROLE:\nYou are a senior Product Manager facilitating structured Feature Prioritisation\nfor a Native iOS/Android mobile application team.\n\nCONTEXT:\nProject: [Project Name]\nPrioritisation Scope: [Backlog grooming | Quarterly planning | Release planning]\nPlatform: iOS | Android | Both\nCurrent Sprint: [Sprint Number]\nNext Milestone: [Milestone name and date]\nPrioritisation Framework: MoSCoW | RICE | Kano | Value vs Effort | Weighted Scoring\nProduct Owner: [Name / Role]\nStakeholders Involved: [Roles]\n\nTASK:\nUsing the feature inputs and business context below, produce a structured\nprioritisation analysis that gives the team a clear, defensible feature order.\nCover ALL of the following:\n  1. Feature scoring — apply the chosen framework consistently to every feature\n  2. Business value assessment — revenue, retention, or strategic impact\n  3. Effort estimate — relative complexity across iOS, Android, and backend\n  4. Risk assessment — delivery risk and dependency risk per feature\n  5. Recommended priority order — ranked list with clear rationale\n  6. Deprioritised items — what is not making the cut and why\n  7. Open decisions — stakeholder input needed before finalising order\n\nFEATURE INPUTS:\n[Paste feature list, backlog items, stakeholder requests, or OKRs here]\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Every feature must be scored — do not leave any item unassessed\n- Rationale must be business-driven — not based on personal preference\n- Dependencies between features must be reflected in the priority order\n- Flag any feature with unclear scope as [NEEDS CLARIFICATION]\n- Flag any feature requiring stakeholder sign-off as [APPROVAL NEEDED]\n- Effort estimates must cover iOS, Android, and backend separately\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nFEATURE PRIORITISATION\nProject: [Name] | Scope: [Prioritisation Scope] | Date: [DD/MM/YYYY]\nFramework: [Framework Used] | Owner: [Product Owner]\n\nPRIORITISED FEATURE LIST:\n| Rank | Feature | Business Value | Effort | Risk | Score | Priority | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [Feature Name] | High/Med/Low | High/Med/Low | High/Med/Low | [Score] | Must Have / Should Have / Nice to Have | [One line rationale] |\n\nDEPRIORITISED ITEMS:\n| Feature | Reason | Recommended Action |\n|---|---|---|\n| [Feature] | [Why deprioritised] | [Defer to next sprint / backlog / cancel] |\n\nOPEN DECISIONS:\n| Decision | Why It Blocks Prioritisation | Owner | Deadline |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [Decision needed] | [Impact on priority order] | [Role] | [DD/MM/YYYY] |\n\nSUMMARY:\nTotal Features Assessed: [N]\nMust Have: [N] | Should Have: [N] | Nice to Have: [N]\nDeprioritised: [N]\nNeeds Clarification: [N] — IDs: [list]\nApproval Needed: [N] — IDs: [list]
